Nearly 70% of illegal aliens ICE arrested across the country have criminal convictions or pending criminal charges in the U.S. alone

WASHINGTON –– U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) arrested more criminal illegal aliens across the country convicted of heinous crimes including sexual abuse of a child, rape, and assault of a family member.

> Yesterday, the heroic men and women of ICE arrested multiple child predators, rapists, domestic abusers, and other heinous criminals,

said Acting Assistant Secretary Lauren Bis.

> Under President Trump and Secretary Mullin, criminal illegal aliens are not welcome in the United States. If you come to our country illegally and break our laws, we will arrest you, deport you, and you will never return.

Yesterday’s arrests include:

Image

Oscar Edgardo Rogel-Gomez, a criminal illegal alien from El Salvador, convicted for sexual abuse of a child in St. George, Utah.

Image

Alcides Ordonez-Cruz, a criminal illegal alien from Honduras, convicted for third-degree gross sexual imposition and endangering children in Van Wert County, Ohio.

Image

Jose Gonzalez-Diaz, a criminal illegal alien from El Salvador, convicted for rape in Riverhead, New York.

Image

Jose Vazquez-Cardoza, a criminal illegal alien from El Salvador, convicted for rape in Riverhead, New York.

Image

Jose Simaj-Barrera, a criminal illegal alien from Guatemala, convicted for assault of a family member in Harris County, Texas.

Americans can see more public safety threats arrested in their communities on our webpage WOW.DHS.Gov.

